asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{18}=3\\sqrt{2},\\,b=\\sqrt{81}=9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{9}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063772/state.json" "file_sha256" "cabb9dce3c706f2d069f1376fc989fb008f9b83c8f1c9fdbf703c3c0a407da1f"} {"question" "q-84084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063772/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3ed0db2ee72af1d9cc1a7e87d55ff89b499ad9ec994545431b201b2611aa4988"} {"question" "q-84084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063772/state.json" "file_sha256" "cabb9dce3c706f2d069f1376fc989fb008f9b83c8f1c9fdbf703c3c0a407da1f"} {"question" "q-84084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{2}{3}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{3}{2}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{9}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063772/state.json" "file_sha256" "cabb9dce3c706f2d069f1376fc989fb008f9b83c8f1c9fdbf703c3c0a407da1f"} {"question" "q-84084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063772/state.json" "file_sha256" "cabb9dce3c706f2d069f1376fc989fb008f9b83c8f1c9fdbf703c3c0a407da1f"} {"question" "q-116564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $8{y}^{2}-25{x}^{2}=200.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063772/state.json" "file_sha256" "cabb9dce3c706f2d069f1376fc989fb008f9b83c8f1c9fdbf703c3c0a407da1f"} {"question" "q-116564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $200$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{y}^{2}-25{x}^{2} & =200 \\\\ \\frac{8{y}^{2}}{200}-\\frac{25{x}^{2}}{200} & =\\frac{200}{200} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt{25}=5,$ and $b=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{2}}x=\\pm \\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{4}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063772/state.json" "file_sha256" "cabb9dce3c706f2d069f1376fc989fb008f9b83c8f1c9fdbf703c3c0a407da1f"} {"question" "q-116564" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063772/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3ed0db2ee72af1d9cc1a7e87d55ff89b499ad9ec994545431b201b2611aa4988"} {"question" "q-116564" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063772/state.json" "file_sha256" "cabb9dce3c706f2d069f1376fc989fb008f9b83c8f1c9fdb